## Deployment Steps

### 1. Push to GitHub
```bash
git init   # if not already
git add .
git commit -m "feat: production deployment"
git remote add origin https://github.com/you/medinsight.git
git push -u origin main
```

### 2. Deploy Backend → Railway
1. [railway.app](https://railway.app) → New Project → Deploy from GitHub repo
2. Select the `backend/` directory (set **Root Directory** = `backend`)
3. Add environment variables:
   - `DATABASE_URL` = your Neon connection string
   - `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` = `https://your-app.vercel.app` *(update after Vercel deploy)*
4. Railway auto-detects `Procfile` and starts the server
5. Copy the generated Railway URL (e.g. `https://medinsight-backend.railway.app`)

### 3. Deploy Frontend → Vercel
1. [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) → New Project → Import GitHub repo
2. Set **Root Directory** = `frontend`
3. Add environment variable:
   - `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` = your Railway backend URL
4. Deploy — Vercel auto-detects Next.js

### 4. Update CORS
After both are deployed, go back to Railway → add:
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` = `https://your-app.vercel.app` (exact Vercel URL)

---

## Verification Plan

### API Health Check
Visit `https://your-backend.railway.app/docs` — all 10 endpoints should be visible.

### End-to-End Browser Test
1. Open your Vercel URL
2. Patient Portal → Register → get Patient ID
3. Browse Departments → see real DB data
4. Book Appointment → get Appointment ID
5. Doctor Portal → Register → get Doctor ID
6. Record Visit using Appointment ID + Patient ID
7. Add Prescription + Treatment using Visit ID
